// The harness has its own workspace, and that is the whole answer to the
// `replace` question (see README.md in this directory).
//
// The repository root's go.work lists exactly the four shipped modules, and
// CI asserts that list equals the `driver/*/go.mod` glob, so adding ./bench to
// it would fail the "go.work uses every discovered module" step. A workspace
// here instead resolves core and the two drivers sibling-on-disk for anything
// run from this directory, leaves the root workspace untouched, and keeps this
// module's go.mod free of the `replace` directive ADR-0002 forbids.
go 1.27

toolchain go1.27rc2

use (
	.
	..
	../driver/env
	../driver/yaml
)
